docs/plans/2026-06-09-001-feat-unified-twofield-solver-plan.md:251:- **Coarse-seed convergence is the novel bet (highest risk).** The PB-MPM 3D-convergence fix this implements has no published reference implementation. Mitigation: it is the *first* gated unit after transfers (U3), the gate is quantitative (divergence-floor curve), and by explicit decision a gate failure halts for redesign rather than silently shipping a compressible-looking fluid. Watch specifically for coarse/fine operator inconsistency reproducing the A≠D·G floor — the gate is designed to catch exactly this.
docs/plans/2026-06-09-001-feat-unified-twofield-solver-plan.md:265:- Exact cavity-gate thresholds (depth multiple, persistence frames) — calibrated empirically ABOVE the pre-committed U4 floors, which are fixed before implementation; empirics may only tighten, never loosen.
