docs/plans/2026-06-18-001-feat-twofield-surface-weighted-dissipation-plan.md:95:### U2. Surface-weighted velocity-averaging dissipation in `g2p_water` (core)
docs/plans/2026-06-18-001-feat-twofield-surface-weighted-dissipation-plan.md:100:- **Files:** `src/solvers/twofield/transfers.wgsl` (`g2p_water`), `tests/twofield_settled.rs`, `tests/twofield_full.rs` (crater decouple), `tests/twofield_water.rs`.
docs/plans/2026-06-18-001-feat-twofield-surface-weighted-dissipation-plan.md:101:- **Approach:** `v = mix(v_own, v_grid, c)` with `v_own = vel[p] + gravity·dt` and `c = smooth_strength(merge_signal, density)` per KTD1/KTD2: dissipate (`c → 1`) when the merge discriminator fires (compressive `div < 0` and/or fast relative-approach into a dense slow neighborhood), preserve (`c → c_surface`) only for separating/coherent-free motion; density is a secondary gate. Gather the mass gradient `grad_m` in the existing g2p loop for the directional approach signal (no new buffer). Damp the affine `C` **proportional to the preserve amount**: `C *= 1 − k·(1−c)` — bulk `c=1` ⇒ `C` unchanged (= current `C = B·dinv·(1−pic_blend)`); strong preserve ⇒ `C` shed by ~`k` (mirrors the prototype's `affine_damp`). Reduce-to-current in the bulk.
docs/plans/2026-06-18-001-feat-twofield-surface-weighted-dissipation-plan.md:102:- **Technical design (directional):** `div = dinv·(b0.x + b1.y + b2.z)`, `dinv = 4/h²` (= `trace(C)`, the local ∇·v; `B` alone is not the gradient). `approach = max(0, dot(v_own − v_grid, normalize(grad_m + ε)))` from the gathered mass gradient `grad_m = Σ(∇w)·grid_vel.w`; `merge = max(−div·div_scale, approach·approach_scale)` — the `approach` term is the robust one (post-projection `div` is weak); the `div_scale ≤ 0` runtime sentinel disables the merge term (the density-only R5 control). `c = clamp(max(merge_to_c(merge), c_surface), c_surface, 1)`. A slow drip merging into the pool fires `approach` even when `div≈0` ⇒ `c→1` ⇒ dissipated **regardless of its own low density**; crown/coherent-free ⇒ `merge≈0` ⇒ `c→c_surface` ⇒ preserve. Tune `div_scale`, the approach term, `c_surface`, and the density gate against the visual oracle; **lock with the R5 telemetry gate**, not by asserting structurality.
docs/plans/2026-06-18-001-feat-twofield-surface-weighted-dissipation-plan.md:114:- **Goal:** Let the surface crown's peak velocity survive the `max_speed` cap without losing the fixed-point overflow guarantee.
docs/plans/2026-06-18-001-feat-twofield-surface-weighted-dissipation-plan.md:117:- **Files:** `src/solvers/twofield/transfers.wgsl` (p2g + g2p clamp sites), `src/solvers/twofield/coupling.wgsl` (`drag_fold` clamp), `src/solvers/twofield/plasticity.wgsl` (`solid_update` clamp), `src/utils/config.rs` / `mod.rs` (cap value), `tests/twofield_water.rs` (overflow + cap-hit probe).
docs/plans/2026-06-18-001-feat-twofield-surface-weighted-dissipation-plan.md:118:- **Approach:** Apply the **water-splash cap** (the `flip.w` lane / Config from U1) at **all three water-path clamp sites** — `p2g_water`, `g2p_water` (`transfers.wgsl`), AND the **water-grid clamp in `drag_fold`** (`coupling.wgsl:292`), which runs *before* project/g2p and would otherwise clip the crown at the global 12. **Leave the solid clamps (`solid_update`, `g2p_solid`) on the global `params.max_speed`** so grain dynamics are unperturbed. Keep the encode-time magnitude clamp as the backstop, **re-derive the FP overflow headroom against the water cap** (∝ `8192/cap`), and add a cap-hit-rate metric + FP-saturation probe so a relaxation that courts i32 overflow fails as a regression, not ships.
docs/plans/2026-06-18-001-feat-twofield-surface-weighted-dissipation-plan.md:121:  - FP-saturation probe: at the chosen **water cap**, encoded node lanes stay below the i32 overflow bound across the violent-pour scene; the global `max_speed` (drag/solid) is unchanged. *(edge: overflow)*
