docs/plans/2026-06-06-006-feat-water-grain-coupling-physics-plan.md:146:**Files:** `src/solvers/xpbd/coupling.wgsl` (`compute_fractions`, `porosity_drag_factor`), `src/solvers/xpbd/common.wgsl` (Params: `coupling_h`), `src/solvers/xpbd/mod.rs` (`h_c`, `cell_size = max(h_c, grain_diameter, h)`, neighbor-count diagnostics), `src/models/mod.rs` (Materials: `coupling_radius` or derived), `tests/xpbd_coupling.rs`.
docs/plans/2026-06-06-006-feat-water-grain-coupling-physics-plan.md:148:**Approach:** `α_s`/drag porosity gather over `h_c ≈ 2–3× grain_diameter`; the water PBF density gather still distance-culls to `h` even though the grid cell is larger (the cell only widens the candidate list). Clamp `ε ∈ [0.35, 0.999]` at use. Add avg/max neighbor-count instrumentation per pass. Legacy single-resolution scenes stay byte-stable when `h_c` resolves to the prior radius.
docs/plans/2026-06-06-006-feat-water-grain-coupling-physics-plan.md:155:- Water PBF unaffected: density residual on a pure-water dam unchanged when only `h_c` differs (PBF still uses `h`).
docs/plans/2026-06-06-006-feat-water-grain-coupling-physics-plan.md:159:**Verification:** smooth bounded porosity with fine water; water PBF + legacy scenes unaffected; neighbor counts observable.
docs/plans/2026-06-06-006-feat-water-grain-coupling-physics-plan.md:173:**Approach:** Keep the existing drag scaffold; fix the coefficient (KTD-3). `compute_coupling_scale` stores `coupling_scale = vec2(β_i, N_i)` — the per-particle Darcy rate from local `ε_i` and the opposite-phase neighbor count (KTD-8; no new binding, drag passes stay 8/8). `drag_delta_for_pair` forms the **symmetric capped pair scale** `s_ij = min(β_max/max(N_i,N_j), harmonic(β_i,β_j)·V_pair·dt)` and returns `s_ij·(m_j/(m_i+m_j))·(vf_j−vf_i)`, summed over neighbors and **Jacobi-subiterated** K times — symmetric (conserving) + per-neighbor capped (aggregate-bounded, no over-damping) + bounded-blend (implicit, no overshoot, no literal `exp()`). Size `β`/`β_max` so a fine bed is cap-limited (the fix for the ~5e-4 bug). Accumulate a **drag-only** work signal for the wake gate (KTD-9). Resolution-normalize so per-grain total drag is invariant under water refinement (KTD-3). Calibrate (with U6 bands) so pour-zone impulse exceeds the friction-budget yield resistance while bulk stays sub-fluidization (KTD-4). Buoyancy untouched; drag uses relative velocity only (KTD-7). Exclusion still present this unit (removed in U2).
docs/plans/2026-06-06-006-feat-water-grain-coupling-physics-plan.md:202:**Approach:** Remove the exclusion passes/params. Retention adds **no new force** (KTD-2): the minimum-porosity floor in the water density target (pure PBF, static, momentum-conserving) keeps water from over-packing into grain space, and the strong drag (U3) slows a moving wetting front to the Darcy velocity. **No `∇α_s` body force** — that would add a pressure channel conflicting with buoyancy (KTD-7). Ensure no stale grain `dp` is applied in the water loop (grains a clean no-op there; bed loop owns grain position). Water threads pores via the floored density field + drag, never collision. Because U3 lands first, the drag is already present when exclusion is removed.
docs/plans/2026-06-06-006-feat-water-grain-coupling-physics-plan.md:250:**Approach:** Water spacing `< grain_diameter` (grain ≈ 2–3× water) at a modest count (defer 200k). Confirm grid (U1) covers the disparity. Run the spacing-invariance gate; keep `max_correction_ratio`; auto-scale substeps if CFL demands. Because U3 resolution-normalized drag, per-grain forcing is invariant across refinement.
docs/plans/2026-06-06-006-feat-water-grain-coupling-physics-plan.md:281:- **Buoyancy/drag decoupling:** hydrostatic saturated bed at rest → zero net grain accel beyond buoyancy balance; flowing bed → drag from relative velocity only (no double-count).
