    81	**The fix — compacted pocket list (the R9 blocker, resolved):** `bubble_fine`/`bubble_coarse`
    82	were a SINGLE-workgroup, ALL-cells reduction (one GPU core strided over ~76k fine cells per
    83	dispatch to sum the few hundred CELL_POCKET rows), run 56×/frame (8 sweeps × 7 substeps) — it was
    84	**78–81 % of the 200k frame**. The flood-fill already labels the pocket cells; the fix builds a
    85	**compacted list** of those indices once per frame via an atomic append folded into the existing
    86	passes (no new dispatches): `flood_init` zeroes two atomic counters (binding 26 `pocket_f`,
    87	binding 27 `pocket_c`); `pocket_mark` appends each fine CELL_POCKET cell; `coarse_cell_setup`
    88	appends each coarse one. The bubble row solves then stride the few-hundred-entry list instead of
    89	all cells — **same λ_b math, same contributing cells, same operator** (only the summation order
    90	differs at float-associativity level; the cavity/crater gates have wide bands and stayed green).
    91	Single-workgroup shape and barrier discipline are preserved (uniform trip count over the list).
    92	Result: bubble_fine fell from ~80 % to **34.5 %** of the frame, and the 200k median dropped from
    93	~68–180 ms to **25.4 ms**. Per-pass breakdown at 200k (substeps-scaled): `bubble_fine` 34.5 %,
    94	`jacobi_fine` 26.4 %, `flood_sweep` 7.5 %, `p2g_water` 5.9 %, `g2p_water` 4.4 %, everything else
    95	< 5 %. The earlier open-cavity early-out (`bubble[2]` flag) is retained on top — it skips the
    96	solve entirely on open-surface frames.
    97	
    98	**Remaining headroom (not needed for the gate):** `bubble_fine` is still the single largest pass.
    99	Further wins if ever needed: a multi-workgroup partial-sum reduction (the list-strided
   100	single-workgroup form is the simplest sufficient fix and was chosen for that reason), or warm-
   101	starting λ_b. These are CK-MPM / kernel-fusion backlog territory; the gate is met without them.
   102	
   103	Offline grid-refinement (GCI, reduced 3×2:1 with budget-scaled fine sweeps) on a settled
   104	hydrostatic column converges cleanly: water-COM height 8.42 → 8.73 → 8.90 su, **observed order
   105	p ≈ 0.82**, Richardson-extrapolated 9.12 su, GCI(fine) 3.2 % — the truncation-error study is in
